The class constructs its own concrete dependencies (S3 client, DB connection) inside the logic and mixes parsing, business rules and I/O in one method (SRP + DIP violations). Inject the dependencies and extract the pure part:

```python
def parse(body: bytes) -> list[list[str]]:
    return [l.split(",") for l in body.decode().splitlines()[1:]]

def non_zero(rows):
    return [r for r in rows if float(r[2]) != 0]

class SettlementProcessor:
    def __init__(self, source, sink):
        self.source, self.sink = source, sink
    def run(self, key):
        self.sink.write(non_zero(parse(self.source.read(key))))

# edge: SettlementProcessor(S3Source(boto3.client('s3'), 'reports'), PgSink(pool))
# test: SettlementProcessor(FakeSource(b'...'), FakeSink())
